WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.000
After Ming Taizu Zhu Yuanzhang passed away, the young imperial grandson Zhu Yunwen ascended the throne as emperor.

2
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:11.600
The little emperor was very young and looked nervous, while the officials knelt and bowed neatly in ceremony.

3
00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:16.760
Emperor Jianwen carried out a policy of reducing the princes' power, which caused strong resentment from Zhu Di, Prince of Yan.

4
00:00:16.760 --> 00:00:21.880
The map marked the fiefs of princes in different places, each more powerful than the last.

5
00:00:21.880 --> 00:00:28.440
In the year 1399, Zhu Di, aged forty, raised troops and marched south under the banner of the Jingnan Campaign.

6
00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:33.400
The Prince of Yan's army was strictly disciplined, and every soldier was full of energy.

7
00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:39.880
The two armies fought for several years, with banners flying and the dust of the march filling the sky.

8
00:00:39.880 --> 00:00:45.160
The soldiers marched in neat steps, and the long column stretched on with no end in sight.

9
00:00:45.160 --> 00:00:50.240
Zhu Di's army finally broke into Nanjing, and Emperor Jianwen disappeared from then on, his fate a mystery.

10
00:00:50.240 --> 00:00:54.920
In the empty palace, only the sound of wind blowing through the windows remained.

11
00:00:54.920 --> 00:00:59.240
Zhu Di ascended the throne as emperor; he was the later Ming Chengzu, the Yongle Emperor.
